    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certifies that on 28 June 2007, the erection of a roof extension, comprising the conversion of the hipped roof to a gabled end and a rear dormer, and the installation of two roof lights to the front roof, as shown on drawing numbers MS/SB/214/07A received 28 June 2007, adding a volume of 27.0m3 to the house, was lawful within the meaning of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reason:\r\n\r\nFollowing the proposed development, the resulting building would fall within the provisions of Schedule 2, Part 1, Class B, of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995.\r\n"
